{{clipping|en|metropolitan}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈmɛt/|a=UK}}
* {{homophones|en|met}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛt|s=1}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-prop|head=the Met}}

# {{lb|en|London|rail transport}} The [[London Underground]] {{w|Metropolitan line}}.
#: {{syn|en|Metropolitan}}
# {{lb|en|London|rail transport|historical|1863–1933}} The {{w|Metropolitan Railway}}.
#: {{syn|en|Metropolitan}}
# {{lb|en|London|law enforcement}} The {{w|Metropolitan Police Service}} of London ([[MPS]]).
#: {{syn|en|Metropol}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-england-london-68786745|title=Westminster murder inquiry: Woman, 27, named by police|first=Victoria|last=Cook|date=2024-04-11|work=bbc.com|text=The Metropolitan Police has referred itself to the Independent Office for Police Conduct (IOPC) over its handling of the investigation. {{...}} The '''Met''' said it had informed its own Directorate of Professional Standards and a "mandatory referral will be made to the IOPC in relation to the initial contact from the woman's friend".|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20240421043503/https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-england-london-68786745|archivedate=21 April 2024}}
# {{lb|en|US}} The {{w|Metropolitan Museum of Art}} in [[New York City]].
#* {{RQ:en:New York Times|date=2022-09-07|author=Gillian Brassil|title=The Real Lives of Early 20th-Century Celebrities, as Depicted in ‘Ragtime’|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/07/t-magazine/ragtime-novel-characters-real.html|passage=Freud’s itinerary in the novel hews neatly to what he and his colleagues really did on their trip to the U.S.: They visited Chinatown and Central Park and the '''Met'''. They made it down to Coney Island, though Jung and Freud’s boat ride through the Tunnel of Love seems to be a Doctorowian flight of fancy.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20221103004436/https://www.nytimes.com/2022/09/07/t-magazine/ragtime-novel-characters-real.html}}
# {{lb|en|New York|arts}} The current or historical {{w|Metropolitan Opera House}} or its opera company.

